# Netlify redirects.
#
# The deploy subdomain still serves a complete, working copy of the site, so
# there are two hosts answering 200 for every page. Both already declare
# brilliancychess.com as canonical, which is enough to stop them competing in
# search — but a canonical is a hint and a 301 is not, and there is no reason
# for the second host to exist at all now that the custom domain is live.
#
# This matters more here than on most sites: the whole SEO position rests on
# brilliancychess.com being an exact-match domain for "brilliancy chess", and an
# earlier version of the head tags pointed the canonical at this subdomain
# instead -- which would have told Google to index the subdomain and left the
# custom domain competing with a host it had itself nominated. That is fixed,
# and this closes the remaining ambiguity rather than relying on the fix.
#
# `!` forces the rule even though a file exists at the path, which is exactly
# the case here: every path on the subdomain resolves.
https://brilliancy-chess.netlify.app/*  https://brilliancychess.com/:splat  301!
